{
    //Guides
      "expandedfoodsguide-title": "Expanded Foods: Cooking 101 - The Basics",
      "expandedfoodsguide-text": "<strong>Expanded Foods: Chef's Cookbook</strong><br><i>Getting started.</i><br><br>Documentation on this mod can be found <a href=\"https://www.vintagestory.at/forums/topic/3783-expanded-foods-123/\">here.</a><br>Updated versions can be found <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/28#description\">here.</a><br><strong>REQUIRES 'A CULINARY ARTILLERY' MOD TO FUNCTION</strong><br><br><strong>Introduction</strong><br>This mod adds a wide variety of uses for food that will make your cooking experience more in-depth. It also interacts with the mods <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/259/\">Acorns</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/487\">Alchemy</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/371/\">Braziers</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/moreanimals/\">More Animals</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/1238/\">Primitive Survival</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/450\">SuperFuel</a> for even more recipes. Wild Farming is also highly recommended, since without it you cannot grow seaweed.<br><i>This mod includes the ability to make bushmeat meals, vinegar and salt. Delete those mods if you are using this one.</i><br><br><strong><i>COOKING BLOCK INFO</i></strong><br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:bottle-clay-blue-corked\">Bottles</a></strong><br>Bottles are used for drizzling syrups or sauces on food via the mixing bowl, fermenting drinks, or simply drinking.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:meathooks-aged-copper-east\">Meat Rack</a></strong><br>Sausage or raw meat (but not fish) can be Dried on a meat rack. This process ages the meat and boosts its nutritional value. Raw aged meat needs to have the exterior cut away before cooking. You can also hang some items such as mini-cauldrons and cleavers.<br>All forms of meat can be Cooked or Baked.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:saucepan-raw\">Saucepan</a></strong><br>Functions somewhat similarly to a bucket, but you can place it onto a firepit to Boil the liquids inside, turning sap and juice into syrup. In order to Boil something in the saucepan, it must be placed into its slots.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:spile-copper-north\">Spile</a></strong><br>Jam this into a tree and place a bucket or saucepan beneath it to collect sap from the tree during certain times of the year.<br><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:maplesapportion\">Maple Sap</a> can be collected from maple trees in January, February, and March.<br><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:birchsapportion\">Birch Sap</a> can be collected from birch trees in April, May, and June.<br><br><strong><i>BASIC FOOD LIST</i></strong><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-egg-chicken-boiled\">Boiled Eggs</a></strong><br>Boil 1 raw egg and 0.5 L of water. Can be used in salads and cold pasta meals.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-egg-chicken-pickled\">Pickled Eggs</a></strong><br>Seal 1 boiled egg and 0.1 L of vinegar in a barrel. Can be used in salads and cold pasta meals.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:limeegg-chicken\">Water-Glassed Eggs</a></strong><br>Seal 1 raw egg with 0.1 L of slaked lime in a barrel. Functionally identical to raw eggs. Can be re-sealed in the barrel to last longer.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:breadcrumbs-spelt\">Bread Crumbs</a></strong><br>You can tear a loaf of bread up in the Crafting Grid or place it in a quern to make bread crumbs out of it. When used in meals, a single portion of bread crumbs gives as much nutrition as 1/4th of a basic loaf of bread.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:candiedfruit-cranberry\">Candied Fruit</a></strong><br>Boil 1 fresh fruit with 0.1 L of its corresponding syrup. Candied fruit can be eaten on its own or added to fruit bread/muffins.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fruitleather-sliced\">Fruit Leather</a></strong><br>After juicing fruit, simmer the mash with 0.1 L of water and 0.2 L of sweetener. Fruit leather can be added to trail mix<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:dryfruit-cranberry\">Dried Fruit</a></strong><br>Bake fruit to preserve them. Dried fruit can be added to any meal that accepts fruit.<br><strong>Meat Variants</strong><br>Hit any meat with a stone or hammer to produce a <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:meatnugget-redmeat-smashed\">smashed</a> version of that meat. Slice the tenderized meat up with a knife or cleaver to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:meatnugget-redmeat-raw\">meat nuggets</a>. This can be done with fish as well, and can be used in any meals that allow regular meat. You can also hang meat from a <a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:meathooks-aged-copper-east\">meat rack</a> to <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:agedmeat-redmeat-normal\">Dry Age</a> it, which needs to have the outside cut off before cooking.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-salt\">Salt</a></strong>Salt now heals 0.5-1 HP when used in food.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-vinegarportion\">Vinegar</a></strong><br>Can be made by sealing fresh berries in a barrel for 28 days, or by letting wine rot instead of cure. 3 fresh fruits can be sealed with 1 L sealed with vinegar as well - it takes a fraction of the time.<br><br><strong>New Vegetable Variants</strong><br>Cook or Bake <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:cookedveggie-cabbage-perfect\">veggies</a> to boost its nutrition and shelf life. Great way to extend the life of veggies that are about to rot. Veggies and mushrooms can also be <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:choppedvegetable-flyagaric\">chopped</a> with a knife or cleaver to make them easier to eat, and chopped mushrooms can be eaten normally.<br><br><strong>BOILING FOOD</strong><br>You can boil eggs, meat, fish, sausage, mushrooms, or vegetables in the saucepan at a ratio of 1 item per 0.5 L of water. This progresses it to the next cooked stage instead of simply charring it.<br><br><strong>FRYING FOOD</strong><br>You can boil any breaded item with 0.1 L of food oil or lard in the saucepan to fry it perfectly every time. Ideal if you hate baking.",
    
      "expandedfoodsguide2-title": "Expanded Foods: Cooking 102 - Expanded Foods",
      "expandedfoodsguide2-text": "<strong>Cooking 102 - Expanded Foods</strong><br><i>Cuisine for the discerning palate.</i><br><br>Documentation on this mod can be found <a href=\"https://www.vintagestory.at/forums/topic/3783-expanded-foods-123/\">here.</a><br>Updated versions can be found <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/28#description\">here.</a><br><br><strong><i>EXPANDED FOOD LIST</i></strong><br><br>All Expanded Foods are Kneaded in a Mixing Bowl.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-bread-flax-perfect\">Bread</a></strong><br><i>0.1 L of water OR milk OR pasteurized milk OR soy milk OR broth<br>1 bag of flour<br>0.1 L of Food Oil or Lard (optional)<br>0.1 L Bread Starter (optional)</i><br>Bake, Cook, or use as pie crust.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:breadedmeatnugget-flax-bushmeat-smashed\">Breaded Food</a></strong><br><i>0.1 L of egg white/egg yolk/liquid egg OR 0.1 liters of honey OR food oil OR birch syrup OR maple syrup OR lard<br>1 handful of bread crumbs<br>1 bag of flour<br>1 handful of smashed fish/meat or fish/meat nuggets OR 1 vegetable/chopped handful of vegetables OR 1 handful of rice grain OR 1 slice of cheese OR 1 boiled/pickled egg.<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>When you have breaded your food, you can Knead it with 0.1 L of food oil or lard to 'deep fry' it, or you can Boil it with 0.1 L of food oil or lard. Once Cooked, Baked, or Boiled, Knead 0.1 L of honey, soy sauce, fish sauce, birch syrup, maple syrup, peanut butter, or peanut sauce in the mixing bowl.<br>Can be used in salads or cold pasta meals.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:candy-peanut-raw\">Candy</a></strong><br><i>0.1 L of honey OR syrup OR peanut butter<br>0.1 L of peanut paste OR sunflower grain<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Knead in the mixing bowl.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:dumpling-raw\">Dumplings</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of Soft Dough<br>1 handful of fish/meat nuggets OR cheese OR chopped veggies OR soybeans OR cheese slice (optional)<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Can be used in stews and soups, Cooked or Baked.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fruitbar-raw\">Fruit Bar</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of peanuts (regular, cooked, or kernels) OR 1 handful of sunflower grain in 1 slot<br>1 fruits or chopped pumpkin slices<br>1 Non-vegetable gelatin<br>0.1 L of peanut paste OR honey OR syrup<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Knead in the mixing bowl.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:berrybread-cooked\">Fruit Bread</a></strong><br><i>1 ball of dough<br>1 fruits, nuts or chopped pumpkin slices in up to 5 slots<br>Fruit, birch, maple, or honey gelatin (optional)<br></i>Once Baked or Cooked, Knead 0.1 L of syrup, honey, peanut butter, or peanut sauce in the mixing bowl.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:gozinaki-cooked\">Gozinaki</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of peanuts (regular, cooked, or kernels) OR 1 handful of sunflower grain in 1 slot<br>1 portion of honey<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Knead ingredients in the mixing bowl, then Bake. Once baked, add honey, syrup, peanut butter, or peanut sauce to the mixing bowl and Knead with gozinaki for a real treat.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:hardtack-spelt-bake1\">Hardtack</a></strong><br>Knead 1 flour, 0.1 liters of water, and 1 handful of salt. <i>Eggs and Herbs optional.</i> Once Baked, it can be Baked up to 3 more times to crush the moisture and flavor out of it and make it last longer.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:gelatin-blueberry\">Gelatin</a></strong><br>Boil 1 liter of bone broth per 1 bone to make 0.25 L of pre-gelatin. Boil 0.1 liters of pre-gelatin, 1 bone, and 1 liter of water to make raw gelatin.<br>Raw Gelatin can be Boiled with 1 liter of water to make plain gelatin, and 0.1 liter of juice or sauce can be added to make something more flavorful. If you are using syrup, then you will need 2 liters of water, each in a different slot of the saucepan.<br>Can be used in pies.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:muffin-cooked\">Muffin</a></strong><br><i>1 ball of soft dough<br>1 fruits, nuts or chopped pumpkin slices in up to 5 slots<br>1 portion of fruit, birch, maple, or honey gelatin (optional)<br></i>Once Baked or Cooked, Knead 0.1 L of syrup, honey, peanut butter, or peanut sauce in the mixing bowl.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:pasta-dough\">Pasta Dough</a></strong><br><i>1 bag of flour<br>0.1 L of liquid egg OR egg yolk<br></i>Once dough is Kneaded, smash until flat with a hammer or rolling pin and cut into noodles with a knife or cleaver. Noodles can be used in meals or Boiled in a saucepan with 1 liter of water to eat by itself. Alternatively, you can bake them to make them last longer, and then use the dried noodles anywhere you would use the cut ones.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:pemmican-raw\">Pemmican</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of animal fat OR 0.1 L of lard<br>1 fruit in 3 slots<br>1 handful of fish/meat nuggets in 2 slots<br>Salt (optional, replaces fruit)</i><br>Cook or Bake.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:sausage-redmeat-raw\">Sausage</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of animal fat OR 0.1 L of lard<br>1 handful of fish/meat nuggets<br>Cheddar or Blue cheese (optional)<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Can be hung on a meat rack to Dry it before cooking. Usable in pies, meat stews, au gratin, and pilaf. Cooked sausage can be used in salads. Using salt to make it results in sausage that cures over time (best hung from the meat rack).<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:plaindoughball-dough\">Soft Dough</a></strong><br><i>0.1 L of water OR milk OR pasteurized milk OR soy milk OR broth<br>1 bag of flour<br>0.1 L of liquid egg<br>0.1 L of Food Oil or Lard (optional)<br>Yeast Starter (optional)</i><br>Bake, Cook, or use as pie crust.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:stuffedpepper-spelt-raw\">Stuffed Pepper</a></strong><br><i>1 bellpepper<br>1 handful of fish/meat nuggets OR 1 chopped handful of vegetables OR 1 handful of pickled cabbage/bellpeppers OR 1 handful of grain OR 1 portion of cheese OR 1 boiled egg OR 1 handful of dried fruit OR 1 sausage link.<br>0.1 L of egg white/egg yolk/liquid egg OR 0.1 L of honey OR food oil OR birch syrup OR maple syrup OR lard (breading optional)<br>1 handful of bread crumbs (breading optional)<br>1 bag of flour (breading optional)<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>When you have breaded your pepper, you can Knead it with 0.1 L of food oil or lard to 'deep fry' it, or you can Boil it with 0.1 L of food oil or lard. Once Cooked, Baked, or Boiled, Knead 0.1 L of honey, soy sauce, fish sauce, birch syrup, maple syrup, peanut butter, or peanut sauce in the mixing bowl.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:sushi-noveggie-nooil\">Sushi</a></strong><br><i>1 sheet of <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:driedseaweed-edible\">dried seaweed</a><br>1 handful of rice grain<br>1 handful of fish nuggets (optional)<br>1 handful of chopped veggies, soybeans, or pickled cabbage (optional)<br>Salt (optional)</i><br>Knead 0.1 L of honey, soy sauce, fish sauce, birch syrup, maple syrup, or peanut sauce in the mixing bowl after creating the sushi roll.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:trailmixvegetarian-beany\">Trail Mix</a></strong><br><i>1 handful of peanuts (regular, cooked, or kernels) in 1 slot<br>1 handful of soybeans OR 2 cured meat nuggets in 1 slot<br>3 handfuls of dried fruit in 1 slot<br>1 slice of Cheddar or Blue cheese<br></i>Kneaded in the mixing bowl. There are 8 types of trail mix - the vegetarian types (Beany, Cheesy, Fruity, & Nutty) and the non-vegetarian types (Cheesy, Fruity, Meaty, & Nutty). To make a specific variant, add 1 or 2 more slots of any of the previous ingredients (ie. 1 handful of peanuts into 1 or 2 more slots to make Nutty trail mix, 2 cured meat nuggets into 1 or 2 more slots to make Meaty Trail Mix.).<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:yogurt-plain\">Yogurt</a></strong><br>In a saucepan, Boil milk until it is <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:pasteurizedmilkportion\">pasteurized</a>. Seal 1 liter of curdled milk and 4 handfuls of non-dried fruits in a barrel for 24 hours to create 0.25 L of <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:yogurt-starter\">yogurt starter</a>.<br>Knead 0.1 L of pasteurized milk with 0.1 L of yogurt starter to create 0.2 L of <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:yogurt-ferment\">fermented yogurt</a>. Seal it in a barrel or bottle until it becomes plain yogurt. Knead with 0.1 L of syrup or honey to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:yogurt-blueberry\">flavored yogurt</a>.",
    
      "expandedfoodsguide4-title": "Expanded Foods: Cooking 104 - Expanded Liquids",
      "expandedfoodsguide4-text": "<strong>Cooking 104 - Expanded Liquids</strong><br><i>How do I make broth?</i><br><br>Documentation on this mod can be found <a href=\"https://www.vintagestory.at/forums/topic/3783-expanded-foods-123/\">here.</a><br>Updated versions can be found <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/28#description\">here.</a><br><br><strong>Introduction</strong><br>The best thing about liquids is how easy they are to store in bulk. The best long-term storage solution is a <a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:bottle-clay-blue-corked\">bottle</a> within the <a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:bottlerack-acacia-acacia-north\">bottle rack</a>, but the most space-efficient solution is a lidded <a href=\"handbook://block-aculinaryartillery:cauldron-iron\">cauldron</a>.Here are a full list of the liquids you can make in this mod.<br><strong>NOTE:</strong> When placing liquids into things, press CTRL + click to place 1/10th of that container's maximum capacity into the container; ie. 0.1 L for bottles/bowls and 1 L for buckets.<br><br><strong><i>LIQUIDS LIST</i></strong><br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-bone\">Bone Broth</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>100 Protein Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>Boil bones and water in a saucepan at a ratio of 1 bone per 1 liter of water.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-meat\">Meat Broth</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>125 Protein Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>Boil water and part-baked meat in a saucepan at a ratio of 1 meat per 1 liter of water.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-fish\">Seafood Broth</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>100 Protein Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>Boil water and part-baked fish in a saucepan at a ratio of 1 portion per 1 liter of water.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-vegetable\">Vegetable Broth</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>100 Vegetable Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>Boil water and part-baked mushrooms or vegetables in a saucepan at a ratio of 1 vegetable per 1 liter of water.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:clarifiedbrothportion-bone\">Clarified Broth</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>130-155 Vegetable or Protein Satiety; 2 HP</i><br>Boil any broth with liquid egg white in a saucepan at a 10:1 ratio.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:breadstarter-wild\">Bread Starter</a></strong><br>In bread: <i>25 Grain Satiety; 1.5 HP</i><br>Place dried berries/pineapple slices and water in a barrel at a ratio of 6 handfuls of berries/slices per liter of water. Seal for 4 days to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:yeastwaterportion\">yeast water</a>, then Mix in a mixing bowl with 1 bag of flour and 1 handful of salt to make Wild Yeast Starter. Mix 1 liters of yeast starter, 1 liter of water in 2 slots, and 1 bag of flour in 2 slots together in the mixing bowl to create more yeast starter, allowing you to maintain it.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fishsauce\">Fish Sauce</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>50 Protein Satiety</i><br>Seal raw fish or fish nuggets in a barrel at a ratio of 8 salt per 64 raw fish (no less) for 14 days to produce <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fermentedfish-slop\">fermented fish</a>, then Press the resulting pile of fish goo.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:foodoilportion-flax\">Food Oil</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>64 Vegetable Satiety; 0.5 HP</i><br>Place flax grains, rice grains, seeds, soy beans, or olives into a fruit press and Press.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fruitsyrupportion-blueberry\">Fruit Syrup</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>120 Fruit Satiety; 1 or 2 HP</i><br>When drank: <i>800 Fruit Satiety; 1 or 2 HP per liter</i><br>Boil fruit juice in a saucepan; 4 juice reduces to 1 syrup. For <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fruitsyrupportion-saguaro\">cactus syrup</a>, Boil 1 liter of water and 1 portion of saguaro fruit in a saucepan. Heals 2 HP.<br>Can be used in pies.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:lard\">Lard</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>160 Protein Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>Boil 1 handful of fat or block of hardened lard in the saucepan with 0.2 L of water. Lard hardens over time into <a href=\"handbook://item-fat-rendered\">rendered fat</a>.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:soysauce\">Soy Sauce</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>64 Protein Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>In a barrel, soak soybeans in water, one liter of water per soybean portion. Once fully soaked, Cook over a firepit and grind in a quern to make roasted soybean powder. Knead this powder with any grain in a mixing bowl or crafting grid to make soy sauce culture and soak in 1 liter of brine. Once the final soak is done, Press the soy slurry in a fruit press to retrieve soy sauce.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:soymilk-edible\">Soy Milk</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>12 Dairy Satiety; 0.1 HP</i><br>When drank: <i>75 Dairy Satiety; 1 HP per liter</i><br>In a barrel, soak soybeans in water, one liter of water per soybean portion. Once fully soaked, place in the crafting grid to de-shell the soybeans, then mix with 1 liter of water in the crafting grid. Grind mixture in a quern to make a blended soybean mixture. Press to make raw soy milk, then Boil to make edible soy milk.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:birchsapportion\">Tree Sap</a></strong><br>When drank (birch sap only): <i>160 Fruit Satiety per liter</i><br>Jam a spile into a birch/maple tree and place a bucket or saucepan underneath to collect... in certain months. Check Cooking 101 for details.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:treesyrupportion-maple\">Tree Syrup</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>96 Fruit Satiety; 1 HP</i><br>When drank: <i>640 Fruit Satiety; 1 HP per liter</i><br>Boil tree sap in a saucepan; 4 sap reduces to 1 syrup.<br>Can be used in pies.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:vegetablejuiceportion-carrot\">Vegetable Juice</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>300 Vegetable Satiety</i><br>When drank: <i>200 Vegetable Satiety per liter</i><br>Place vegetables into a fruit press and Press.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-vinegarportion\">Vinegar</a></strong><br>In meals: <i>150 Fruit Satiety; 0.5 HP</i><br>Seal wine or spirits in a barrel to let it ferment, or place 3 berries/pineapple slices and 1 L vinegar in a barrel to make it quickly. Takes 2 weeks normally and 1 week the quick way.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:peanutliquid-butter\">Peanut Butter</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>320 Protein Satiety; 60 Vegetable Satiety; 40-120 Fruit Satiety (optional)</i><br>Break peanuts apart in the Crafting Grid to get skins and kernels, then Grind kernels into Peanut Paste. Knead equal portions of peanut paste and food oil to make peanut butter. Honey OR syrup, and salt may also be used when kneading.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:peanutliquid-sauce\">Peanut Sauce</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>220 Protein Satiety; 40-120 Fruit Satiety</i><br>Break peanuts apart in the Crafting Grid to get skins and kernels, then Grind kernels into Peanut Paste. Knead equal portions of peanut paste, soy sauce, honey or syrup, and water to make peanut sauce. Salt may also be used when kneading... 10 salt per 0.1 L of liquid.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:dressing-salad\">Salad Dressing</a></strong><br>In meals or expanded foods: <i>30 Protein Satiety; 104-178 Fruit Satiety; +1-2.5 HP</i><br>Knead equal portion of egg white, food oil, and vinegar. Honey or tree syrup, and salt may also be used when kneading.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:soulstormbrew-basic\">SoulStorm Brew</a></strong><br>When drank: <i>-1000 satiety; +100 HP</i><br>Knead 1 handful of cooked chopped mushrooms (poisonous ones only), 1 handful of bonemeal, 1 handful of saltpeter, 0.1 L of aqua vitae, and 0.1 L of green dye in the mixing bowl to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:soulstormbrew-slop\">SoulStorm Slop</a>. Boil bonemeal and SoulStorm Slop in the saucepan at a ratio of 1 bonemeal per 0.2 L of Slop to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:soulstormbrew-refinedslop\">Refined SoulStorm Slop</a>. Distill in the condenser/boiler to make SoulStorm brew.<br>Soulstorm slop can be put in pies.<br><strong>WARNING:</strong> Drinking SoulStorm brew can result in a satiety deficit. If you get too hungry, just drink more Brew! Drink until you drop!<br><br>These categories apply to the fruit press as well, but you need at least 1 Catfish, 2 Arctic Char/Carp/Perch/Pike/Trout, 4 Bass/Bluegill, or 6 fish fillets.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:acorncoffee\">Acorn Coffee</a> (Acorns Only)</strong><br>Boil 0.5 L of water with 1 portion of Acorn Powder, which is made by grinding up roasted acorns.<br><br><strong>ALCOHOL CHANGES</strong><br>All alcohol in the base game can now spoil into vinegar if left out in the open long enough. Seal them into a cauldron or store them in bottles and they will cure, becoming finer with age. If juice is stored in this way, it will eventually cure into cider.",
    
      "expandedfoodsguide5-title": "Expanded Foods: Cooking 105 - Compatibility",
      "expandedfoodsguide5-text": "<strong>Cooking 105 - Compatibility</strong><br><i>These mods let me make WHAT?</i><br><br>Documentation on this mod can be found <a href=\"https://www.vintagestory.at/forums/topic/3783-expanded-foods-123/\">here.</a><br>Updated versions can be found <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/28#description\">here.</a><br><br><strong>Introduction</strong><br>Expanded Foods has new recipes utilizing aspects from the following mods: <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/259/\">Acorns</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/487\">Alchemy</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/ancienttools/\">Ancient Tools</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/371/\">Braziers</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/moreanimals/\">More Animals</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/1238\">Primitive Survival</a>, <a href=\"https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/450\">SuperFuel</a>. This section details how to make these foods.<br><br><strong><i>ACORNS</i></strong><br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:acornportion\">Handful of Acorns</a></strong><br>Place dry leached acorns onto your crafting grid to split them into managable portions.<br>Acorns may be added to Meat Stews, Porridge, Vegetable Stews, Au Gratin, Pilaf, Salads, and Yogurt. They are interchangable with peanuts in recipes & foods. When making Fruit Bars, Gozinaki or Trail Mix, use 2 handfuls of acorns instead of 1 handful of peanuts. You can also roast them in the firepit.<br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:acorncoffee\">Acorn Coffee</a></strong><br>Boil 0.1 L of water with 1 portion of Acorn Powder, which is made by grinding up roasted acorns.<br>All other Acorns additions simply involve adding Acorn Flour to a recipe that uses flour, or using acorn crumbs in place of regular crumbs.<br><br><strong><i>ANCIENT TOOLS</i></strong><br><br>Salted meat nuggets can be used in place of regular meat nuggets.<br>Animal brains can be used to make fried balls, or used in au gratin, hot pasta, or pilaf.<br><br><strong><i>PRIMITIVE SURVIVAL</i></strong><br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:fishsauce\">Fish Sauce</a></strong><br><i>Barrel portions:</i><br>Bass/Bluegill/fish fillets require 8 salt per 64 fish/fillet.<br>Arctic Char/Carp/Perch/Pike/Trout require 8 salt per 32 fish.<br>Catfish require 8 salt per 16 fish.<br><br><strong><a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-fish\">Seafood Broth</a></strong><br>Part-baked fish filets and crab nuggets can be used in place of part-baked fish.<br><br><i>NOTE</i><br><br>Crab meat is interchangable with fish in all recipes.<br>Snake meat is interchangable with chicken in all recipes.<br>You can use 4 sticks of jerky instead of 2 cured meat nuggets when making trail mix.<br>Smoked meat & cured smoked meat is interchangable with cured meat in all recipes.<br><br><strong><i>BRAZIERS</i></strong><br><br>Food Oil and Lard can be used to create Braziers.<br><br><strong><i>MORE ANIMALS</i></strong><br><br>Weird bird eggs can be used in place of chicken eggs.<br><br><strong><i>SUPERFUELS</i></strong><br><br>Food Oil and Lard can be used to create Fire Logs.",

