    "item-handbooktitle-broth": "Musings On Broth",
    "item-handbooktext-broth": "Broth is an excellent way to stretch out many resources and make them useful for years. By <a href=\"handbook://simmeringguide\">simmering</a> bones, meat, vegetables, or mushrooms in water, wonderful broths can be made. Non-bone broths must be made with partially cooked ingredients, as the roasting process is essential to imparting its flavor onto the water. Broths can be clarified by simmering them with egg white, to coagulate impurities which are then removed by skimming off the top as it cooks.<br>Broth is great in any dough, and it enhances most meals.",

