    "item-handbooktitle-lard": "Lard",
    "item-handbooktext-lard": "Liquid animal fat, rendered by boiling chunks of fat in water. Its property of producing very little smoke when cooked and its flavor makes it ideal for frying foods. The fatty content makes dough more flaky, too.<br>Note: Cooking 1 chunk of fat results in 0.2L of lard, and most recipes in Expanded Foods only require 0.1L of lard - this effectively doubles how much fat you can use in recipes.",
  
