    "item-handbooktitle-gelatin": "Gelatin Production",
    "item-handbooktext-gelatin": "First, <a href=\"handbook://simmeringguide\">simmer</a> bones in water to start releasing the collagens and make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:brothportion-bone\">bone broth</a>. Take that bone broth and simmer it with more bones to start gelatinizing it and reducing its proteins into peptides, creating <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:gelatin-liquid\">pre-gelatin</a>. Finally, simmer pre-gelatin with more bones to create <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:gelatin-raw\">raw gelatin</a>, a flavorless hydrogel. At this point, it can be simmered with any juice or syrup to make <a href=\"handbook://item-expandedfoods:gelatin-saguaro\">flavored gelatin</a>.",
  
  
